print(any_int(3, 2, 2))  # ➞ False
print(any_int(3, -2, 1))  # ➞ True
print(any_int(3.6, -2.2, 2))  # ➞ False
```

This function `any_int` first checks if all three numbers are integers. If they are not, it returns `False`. If they are all integers, it then checks if any of the numbers is equal to the sum of the other two. If such a number exists, it returns `True`; otherwise, it returns `False`.

