    find_max(["name", "enam", "game"]) == "enam"
    find_max(["aaaaaaa", "bb" ,"cc"]) == "aaaaaaa"
    """
    max_word = None

    for word in words:
        unique_chars = set(word)
        if len(unique_chars) > len(unique_chars if max_word else set(max_word)) or (len(unique_chars) == len(unique_chars if max_word else set(max_word)) and word < max_word):
            max_word = word

    return max_word
```

This function should pass the provided tests. It iterates through the list of words, calculates the unique characters in each word, and keeps track of the maximum word accordingly.
