You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a python function to check whether the given number is co-prime or not. Your code should pass these tests:

assert is_coprime(17,13) == True
assert is_coprime(15,21) == False
assert is_coprime(25,45) == False
[BEGIN]

answer:  def is_coprime(a, b):
    return gcd(a, b) == 1

def gcd(a, b):
    while b != 0:
        a, b = b, a % b
    return a

# Test cases
assert is_coprime(17, 13) == True
assert is_coprime(15, 21) == False
assert is_coprime(25, 45) == False

print("All tests passed!")


