You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to find all index positions of the maximum values in a given list. Your code should pass these tests:

assert position_max([12,33,23,10,67,89,45,667,23,12,11,10,54])==[7]
assert position_max([1,2,2,2,4,4,4,5,5,5,5])==[7,8,9,10]
assert position_max([2,1,5,6,8,3,4,9,10,11,8,12])==[11]
[BEGIN]

answer:  def position_max(nums):
    indices = []
    max_value = max(nums)
    for i, num in enumerate(nums):
        if num == max_value:
            indices.append(i)
    return indices

# Tests
assert position_max([12, 33, 23, 10, 67, 89, 45, 667, 23, 12, 11, 10, 54]) == [7]
assert position_max([1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5, 5, 5]) == [7, 8, 9, 10]
assert position_max([2, 1, 5, 6, 8, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 8, 12]) == [11]
