You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to search an element in the given array by using sequential search. Your code should pass these tests:

assert sequential_search([11,23,58,31,56,77,43,12,65,19],31) == (True, 3)
assert sequential_search([12, 32, 45, 62, 35, 47, 44, 61],61) == (True, 7)
assert sequential_search([9, 10, 17, 19, 22, 39, 48, 56],48) == (True, 6)
[BEGIN]

answer:  def sequential_search(arr, target):
    index = 0
    while index < len(arr):
        if arr[index] == target:
            return (True, index)
        index += 1
    return (False, -1)

