You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a function to find the maximum sum possible by using the given equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n). Your code should pass these tests:

assert get_max_sum(60) == 106
assert get_max_sum(10) == 12
assert get_max_sum(2) == 2
[BEGIN]

answer:  def get_max_sum(n):
    if n == 0:
        return 0
    else:
        return max(get_max_sum(n//2) + get_max_sum(n//3) + get_max_sum(n//4) + get_max_sum(n//5), n)

# Test cases
assert get_max_sum(60) == 106
assert get_max_sum(10) == 12
assert get_max_sum(2) == 2
