assert heap_queue_largest( [25, 35, 22, 85, 14, 65, 75, 22, 58],2)==[85, 75] 
assert heap_queue_largest( [25, 35, 22, 85, 14, 65, 75, 22, 58],5)==[85, 75, 65, 58, 35]
[BEGIN]
import heapq as hq
def heap_queue_largest(nums,n):
  largest_nums = hq.nlargest(n, nums)
  return largest_nums
[DONE]

You are an expert Python programmer, and here is your task: Write a python function to find gcd of two positive integers. Your code should pass these tests:

assert gcd(12, 17) == 1
assert gcd(4,6) == 2
assert gcd(2,9) == 1
[BEGIN]

answer:  def gcd(a, b):
    while b != 0:
        a, b = b, a % b
    return a
